	<item>
		<title>By: Sharifa Norton and Muinuddin Smith</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=795&#038;cpage=1#comment-8555</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Sharifa Norton and Muinuddin Smith]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 26 Jun 2011 17:49:12 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=795#comment-8555</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Dear Ramana, your deep hug,  laughter, loving glance and healing balm are ever with us, even as you have journeyed home.  
On the day after you passed, we read your name within Sura Ya Sin, and its translation, RAMANA = Mercy Full, and it read of  &quot;one who is in awe of the Mercy Full in the unseen&quot;.  It is your being!  We are ever grateful for your friendship, guidance and great spirit. 

Love,  
Sharifa and Muinuddin]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Dear Ramana, your deep hug,  laughter, loving glance and healing balm are ever with us, even as you have journeyed home.<br />
On the day after you passed, we read your name within Sura Ya Sin, and its translation, RAMANA = Mercy Full, and it read of  &#8220;one who is in awe of the Mercy Full in the unseen&#8221;.  It is your being!  We are ever grateful for your friendship, guidance and great spirit. </p>
<p>Love,<br />
Sharifa and Muinuddin</p>
]]></content:encoded>
